  "body": "hi there!\n\nFirst of all - thank you for putting all the work into publicai.co - I think it's a really exciting project, and I hadn't realised someone had already combined so many open parts of a stack to provide a real, actually convincing chat service!\n\nI have one question about how inference is served. When I run a request I see this section at the top saying which inference provider is running the inference for the conversation:\n\n<img width=\"850\" height=\"773\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/87083869-e326-4387-a58a-97151c4af771\" />\n\nI was curious, and I came across this section which seems to imply it's more of a random attribution, rather than there being some clever headers tracking which provider is actually serving the inference for a specific conversation:\n\nhttps://github.com/forpublicai/chat.publicai.co/blob/main/community/owui_functions/sponsor_attribution.py#L54-L64\n\nIs it actually possible to tell where the inference is being run when using the current stack?\n\nI can see hints of Kubernetes, LiteLLM, and OpenWebUI in the code base and I'm trying to understand how plausible it would be to provide visibility into the energy and carbon emissions associated with each API request, based on the where inference is being run.",
